<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82740" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετεινός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετηνός</span></b>  (v. fin.), and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτηνός</span></b>  (v. sub voc.), 
			Ep.
		 and poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετεηνός</span></b> 
		(also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετεεινός</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			9.337
		</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
			Leon.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			363.22
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Mel.
		</span></i>)):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>able to
				fly, full-fledged</i>, of young birds, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάρος πετεηνὰ γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.218
				</span></i>
			; of birds generally, <i>able to fly, winged</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετηνῶν . . ὑπ᾽ οἰωνῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					1025
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετηνοῖς γυψί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					515
				</span></i>
			 ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἵππος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Pk.</u>
					342
				</span></i>
			 : abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετεηνά</span>
			<i>winged fowl</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰετὸς . . τελειότατος πετεηνῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.247
				</span></i>
			, al. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετεινόν</span>
			<i>a bird</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				1097
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πετεινά</span> (with 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετηνά</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.140
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.106
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lycurg.
				132
			</span></i>.—Thom.Mag.<i><span class="en">
				p.272
			</span></i> R. rejects the form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετεινός</span> : <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πετηνή</span> is
			the name of an 
				Att.
			ship in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1611.138
			</span></i>.</div>
